  <static seed="40" source="Library/LoyolaChicago/Precalc/Chap3Sec1/Connally3-3-1-19-Exponential-functions.pg">
    <statement><p>Find a formula for <m>P = f(t)</m>, the  size of the population that begins in year
<m>t = 0</m> with <m>2210</m> members and decreases at a <m>3.8</m>%  annual
rate.  Assume that time is measured in years.</p>
<p><m>P = f(t) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2210\cdot 0.962^{t}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The starting value is <m>a=2210</m>. The growth rate is <m>r=-0.038</m>% (note that it is negative), 
so <m>b=1+r=0.962</m>. The formula is</p>
<p><me>P = {2210\cdot 0.962^{t}}</me></p>
</solution>
